  "about": "Sector labels for Morrow's quantum-readiness league (GET /api/public/league, services/league.py). The league list is exactly the explicit 'domains' below, deduplicated; each is graded at most once a week by the public grade (services/public_grade.py) and the table shows only stored results. A domain is labelled by two kinds of rule, in this order: (1) an exact domain in a sector's 'domains' list (a leading 'www.' is ignored); (2) a domain-suffix rule ('suffixes' / 'suffix_patterns') that is reserved for that kind of organisation by its registry. Explicit domains always win over suffix rules; 'exclude' wins over both. Anything not matched is 'unclassified': nothing is guessed. Every explicit domain is the main public domain of a named, publicly known organisation of that sector (company website, annual report or the organisation's Wikipedia article). Nothing is inferred from keywords in the domain name or from page content. Add a domain only when you can name the organisation and its sector from a public source; when unsure, leave it out.",
